WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.758
Doctor and Pharmacy.

2
00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:06.262
Day 42 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Everyday Life phase.

3
00:00:08.012 --> 00:00:09.036
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:17.636
Being precise with a doctor is like writing a good bug report: symptoms, when it started, how bad it is, and what makes it better or worse.

5
00:00:18.986 --> 00:00:19.839
Part 1.

6
00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:21.463
The health bug report.

7
00:00:22.713 --> 00:00:24.591
Here is a template you can copy.

8
00:00:24.871 --> 00:00:28.071
What: sore throat and fever (101 degreesF).

9
00:00:28.351 --> 00:00:29.076
Since:

10
00:00:29.356 --> 00:00:31.148
2 days, started Tuesday night.

11
00:00:31.428 --> 00:00:33.945
Severity: pain 6 or 10 when swallowing.

12
00:00:34.225 --> 00:00:35.655
Pattern: worse at night.

13
00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.007
Tried: paracetamol, helps for ~4 hours.

14
00:00:39.287 --> 00:00:43.127
Other: no allergies; I take blood-pressure medicine (amlodipine).

15
00:00:45.977 --> 00:00:46.851
Part 2.

16
00:00:47.131 --> 00:00:48.241
At the doctor's.

17
00:00:49.491 --> 00:00:50.813
Describing symptoms:

18
00:00:51.093 --> 00:00:52.779
I've had a headache for three days.

19
00:00:53.059 --> 00:00:55.939
It's a sharp or dull or throbbing or burning pain.

20
00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:59.248
It hurts when I bend down or swallow or breathe deeply.

21
00:00:59.528 --> 00:01:02.429
I feel dizzy or nauseous or tired all the time.

22
00:01:02.709 --> 00:01:04.373
I'm allergic to penicillin.

23
00:01:04.653 --> 00:01:06.360
Questions to ask the doctor:

24
00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.289
What do you think is causing this?

25
00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.635
Is it serious?

26
00:01:10.915 --> 00:01:12.089
Is it contagious?

27
00:01:12.369 --> 00:01:15.355
How often should I take this medicine, and for how long?

28
00:01:15.635 --> 00:01:17.833
Are there any side effects I should watch for?

29
00:01:18.113 --> 00:01:20.182
Can I work or travel or exercise?

30
00:01:20.462 --> 00:01:22.766
When should I come back if it doesn't get better?

31
00:01:23.046 --> 00:01:24.411
Do I need any tests?

32
00:01:25.761 --> 00:01:26.657
Part 3.

33
00:01:26.937 --> 00:01:28.004
At the pharmacy.

34
00:01:29.254 --> 00:01:30.918
I have a prescription for this.

35
00:01:31.198 --> 00:01:34.078
Do you have something for a cough or cold or acidity?

36
00:01:34.358 --> 00:01:37.089
Is this safe to take with my blood-pressure medicine?

37
00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:39.438
Should I take it before or after food?

38
00:01:39.718 --> 00:01:41.745
Is there a generic or cheaper version?

39
00:01:43.095 --> 00:01:44.012
Part 4.

40
00:01:44.292 --> 00:01:45.337
Emergencies.

41
00:01:46.587 --> 00:01:47.505
Watch out:

42
00:01:47.785 --> 00:01:49.193
Emergency phrases.

43
00:01:49.473 --> 00:01:50.817
I need an ambulance.

44
00:01:51.097 --> 00:01:53.977
Someone has collapsed at exact address or landmark.

45
00:01:54.257 --> 00:01:56.305
Please call a doctor, it's urgent.

46
00:01:56.585 --> 00:01:59.337
Where is the nearest hospital or emergency room?

47
00:01:59.617 --> 00:02:00.363
India:

48
00:02:00.643 --> 00:02:05.571
112 (all emergencies), 108 (ambulance in many states).

49
00:02:05.851 --> 00:02:15.793
Abroad: learn the local emergency number before you travel (for example, 911 US, 112 EU, 999 UK).

50
00:02:17.143 --> 00:02:18.103
Part 5.

51
00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:19.812
Practice conversations.

52
00:02:21.062 --> 00:02:22.171
At the doctor's.

53
00:02:22.451 --> 00:02:24.478
Here is how the conversation goes.

54
00:02:24.758 --> 00:02:26.166
Good morning.

55
00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:28.003
What brings you here today?

56
00:02:28.283 --> 00:02:29.734
Good morning, doctor.

57
00:02:30.014 --> 00:02:33.193
I've had a sore throat and a fever for two days.

58
00:02:33.473 --> 00:02:35.009
How high is the fever?

59
00:02:35.289 --> 00:02:37.550
It was 101 last night.

60
00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.627
I took a paracetamol, and it came down for a few hours.

61
00:02:42.977 --> 00:02:44.577
The conversation continues.

62
00:02:44.857 --> 00:02:46.585
Any cough or body pain?

63
00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:49.041
A dry cough, and some body ache.

64
00:02:49.321 --> 00:02:50.815
Let me check your throat...

65
00:02:51.095 --> 00:02:52.332
It's an infection.

66
00:02:52.612 --> 00:02:55.236
I'll prescribe an antibiotic for five days.

67
00:02:55.516 --> 00:02:57.948
Should I take it before or after food?

68
00:02:58.228 --> 00:02:59.871
After food, twice a day.

69
00:03:00.151 --> 00:03:01.921
Drink warm water and rest.

70
00:03:03.271 --> 00:03:04.871
The conversation continues.

71
00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.602
Can I go to work?

72
00:03:06.882 --> 00:03:08.226
Rest for two days.

73
00:03:08.506 --> 00:03:11.194
Come back if the fever doesn't go down by Friday.

74
00:03:11.474 --> 00:03:12.839
Thank you, doctor.

75
00:03:14.189 --> 00:03:15.256
At the pharmacy.

76
00:03:15.536 --> 00:03:17.563
Here is how the conversation goes.

77
00:03:17.843 --> 00:03:20.680
Hi, I have a prescription for these medicines.

78
00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.005
Let me see...

79
00:03:22.285 --> 00:03:23.395
We have both.

80
00:03:23.675 --> 00:03:26.128
Do you want the full course of the antibiotic?

81
00:03:26.408 --> 00:03:28.008
Yes, the full five days.

82
00:03:28.288 --> 00:03:30.891
Is there a generic version of the cough syrup?

83
00:03:31.171 --> 00:03:33.432
Yes, it's cheaper and works the same way.

84
00:03:33.712 --> 00:03:35.333
Okay, I'll take that.

85
00:03:35.613 --> 00:03:38.344
Can I take the syrup with the antibiotic?

86
00:03:39.694 --> 00:03:41.294
The conversation continues.

87
00:03:41.574 --> 00:03:42.854
Yes, that's fine.

88
00:03:43.134 --> 00:03:46.057
Just keep two hours between the syrup and any antacid.

89
00:03:46.337 --> 00:03:47.275
Thank you.

90
00:03:47.555 --> 00:03:49.603
Could I have a bill for insurance?

91
00:03:49.883 --> 00:03:51.099
Sure, here it is.

92
00:03:52.449 --> 00:03:53.985
That's the end of this lesson.

93
00:03:54.265 --> 00:03:58.916
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

94
00:03:59.196 --> 00:04:05.319
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

